Ladybird uses a popover’s source as its implicit anchor, and a
pseudo-element uses its originating element. Default-anchor lookup
respects position-anchor: auto, none, and normal; normal enables the
implicit anchor only with a position-area. Explicit names retain
priority. Anchor functions, position-area, and anchor-center use the
same lookup and the same anchor eligibility checks.

Blink sets the relationship in HTMLElement::SetImplicitAnchor. Its
Element::ImplicitAnchorElement also handles originating elements,
and AnchorEvaluatorImpl::ResolveAnchorReference resolves the anchor.
Gecko uses AnchorPositioningUtils::GetUsedAnchorName to select the
default anchor, and GetAnchorPosImplicitAnchor finds its frame. In
WebKit, findImplicitAnchor in AnchorPositionEvaluator.cpp retrieves
the popover invoker or originating element, then checks eligibility.
Ladybird matches those anchor choices and applies the same checks.

Ladybird clears the popover relationship when hiding it. Gecko clears
its invoker in Document’s hide-popover steps, and WebKit clears it in
HTMLElement::hidePopoverInternal. Blink clears the implicit anchor in
Document::RemoveFromTopLayerImmediately. Ladybird follows the current
HTML hide-popover steps by clearing it when removal is requested too.
